WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.954
AI belongs in the architecture as
a component behind one interface,

2
00:00:03.954 --> 00:00:07.300
so providers and models can
change without changing code.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.656
Most uses, like drafting text or
answering from agency content,

4
00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:13.750
change nothing by themselves.

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.062
Agents are different, because they act.

6
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:19.609
You can't count on a model
refusing a hidden instruction,

7
00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:24.621
so the design limits what a steered agent
can do: an identity and a human sponsor,

8
00:00:24.621 --> 00:00:28.862
a short list of allowed tools, a step
limit, and an audit of every call.

9
00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:32.325
And the big one: no agent
writes to a system of record.

10
00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:36.788
It proposes, a person approves,
and the service applies the change.

11
00:00:36.788 --> 00:00:38.380
Next, compliance.
